    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d15">

                <pb facs="0104" n="12" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg12"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President
                        Roosevelt</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d15-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-06-29">29 June 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>To President from former Naval person personal and secret. Number 336.</p>
                <pb facs="0105" n="13" xml:id="pg13"/>
                <p>I have now received your 297 and I repeat what I said in my 334 that if you and
                    Uncle J. can fix a meeting together I should no longer deprecate it. On the
                    contrary in view of his attitude I think it important that this contact should
                    be established.</p>
                <p>I should be very glad to arrange for a meeting between us and our staffs about
                    the end of August in Quebec which I am sure MacKenzie King would welcome. Later
                    on I will put the point to him.</p>
                <p>Many thanks for your very full message.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
